{%- comment %} Cloud providers whose IngressNginxController in the getting started configuration uses inlet HostPort (no nginx-load-balancer Service). {% endcomment %}
{%- assign hostPortInletPlatforms = "vsphere,vcd,zvirt" | split: "," %}
{%- if hostPortInletPlatforms contains page.platform_code %}{% assign ingressInletHostPort = true %}{% else %}{% assign ingressInletHostPort = false %}{% endif %}
{% tabs dns_options %}
{% tab "Wildcard DNS record" %}
Use this option if you have a DNS server and your cluster DNS name template is a [wildcard template](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wildcard_DNS_record) (e.g., `%s.kube.company.my`).

{% if page.platform_code == 'aws' -%}
On the DNS server, add a wildcard CNAME record containing the hostname of the load balancer. To get the hostname of the load balancer:

{% include getting_started/global/partials/GET_BALANCER_ADDR.liquid %}
{%- elsif ingressInletHostPort -%}
On the DNS server, add a wildcard A record containing the IP address of the master node.
{%- else -%}
On the DNS server, add a wildcard A record containing the IP address of the load balancer.
{%- if page.platform_code != 'existing' %} To get the load balancer IP address:

{% include getting_started/global/partials/GET_BALANCER_ADDR.liquid %}
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
{% endtab %}
{% tab "Individual DNS records" %}
Use this option if you have a DNS server and your cluster DNS name template is **not** a [wildcard template](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wildcard_DNS_record) (e.g., `%s-kube.company.my`).

On the DNS server, add {% if page.platform_code == 'aws' %}CNAME records{% else %}A or CNAME records{% endif %} containing the address of {% if ingressInletHostPort %}the master node{% else %}the load balancer{% endif %} for the following DNS names:

<ul>
{%- assign domains = site.data.reference.public-domains %}
{%- for domain in domains %}
{%- if domain.gs %}
<li><b title="E.g., <em>&quot;{{ domain.name }}-kube.company.my&quot;</em><br>for the <em>&quot;%s-kube.company.my&quot; template</em>">{{ domain.name }}</b></li>
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
</ul>

{% alert type="info" %}
The list above contains the DNS names that a cluster deployed using this guide requires. The complete list is given in the [“List of Reserved Deckhouse Platform DNS Names”](/products/kubernetes-platform/documentation/latest/reference/public-domains.html) section of the documentation.
{% endalert %}
{% if page.platform_code == 'aws' %}
To get the hostname of the load balancer:

{% include getting_started/global/partials/GET_BALANCER_ADDR.liquid %}
{%- elsif ingressInletHostPort == false and page.platform_code != 'existing' %}
To get the load balancer IP address:

{% include getting_started/global/partials/GET_BALANCER_ADDR.liquid %}
{%- endif %}
{% endtab %}
{% tab "Hosts file" %}
Use this option if you don't have a DNS server. On the computer from which you need access to Deckhouse services, add static records to the hosts file (`/etc/hosts` for Linux, `%SystemRoot%\system32\drivers\etc\hosts` for Windows).

{% if ingressInletHostPort == false and page.platform_code != 'existing' -%}
To get the IP address of the load balancer, run the following command on the **master node**:

{% include getting_started/global/partials/GET_BALANCER_ADDR.liquid mode="hosts" %}

{% endif -%}
To get the command for adding the records, use the [hosts file data generator](/products/kubernetes-platform/documentation/latest/reference/public-domains.html#hosts-file-data-generator): enter the DNS name template and the IP address of {% if ingressInletHostPort %}the master node{% else %}the load balancer{% endif %}.
{% endtab %}
{% endtabs %}
